{
  "requirement": "Each requirement and example declaration badge has two adjacent links. Its\nkind (`req` or `example`) links to the declaration's anchor on the current\npage; its full name links to the evidence detail page. These segments stay\ntogether in one non-wrapping row, with no separate arrow link or plaintext evidence link.\nEach detail page links back to the declaration's anchored badge and to the\nindex. Reference badges continue to link to the declaration. These links\nresolve when a requirement name contains `.md`, as in\n`requirements.cli.mdbook`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I reviewed only the supplied tests and did not request any implementation source. Together they cover each obligation in `requirements.index.navigation`.\n\n**Two adjacent links in the declaration badge**\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[declaration_sections_contain_their_headers_and_markdown_bodies]` checks the exact header HTML for both a `req` and an `example` declaration.\n  - The kind link is `href=\"#habeas-{kind}-rules.{name}\"` with the text `req` or `example`.\n  - The name link is `habeas-badge-name` with `href=\"requirements-index/rules.{name}.html\"` and the full name as its text.\n  - The test asserts that no `habeas-detail-icon` appears in the header.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages]` and `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons]` check the anchor ids and detail hrefs. They also assert that \"See evidence\" is absent, so there is no plaintext evidence link.\n- `tests/repository.rs#fn[mdbook_preprocessor_renders_definitions_between_stdin_and_stdout]` runs the real preprocessor binary. It checks that each badge row has exactly two `</a>` elements, one `habeas-badge-kind` and one `habeas-badge-name`, with no `<svg`, and with both the anchor and the detail hrefs.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[definition_evidence_link_targets_are_escaped]` checks that the name link target is escaped.\n\n**One non-wrapping row**\n`src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[declaration_badge_stylesheet_keeps_split_links_in_one_row]` asserts `inline-flex`, `flex-wrap: nowrap`, `white-space: nowrap` and `flex-shrink: 0` in the stylesheet. The same test class also asserts that the two segments sit inside one `habeas-definition-badge` span.\n\n**Detail pages link back to the anchored badge and to the index**\n- `fn[index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters]` in `src/index.rs` checks the \"View definition\" link to `../../requirements/core.html#habeas-req-...`. It also checks the \"Requirements index\" link at the start of the page.\n- `fn[detail_pages_link_to_readme_chapters_at_their_index_output]` in `src/index.rs` covers the README-chapter case.\n- `fn[definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages]` checks the index link on every detail page. It also checks the definition links for a nested chapter and a `.md` name.\n- `fn[index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons]` covers an `example` detail page.\n- `fn[detail_pages_rebase_markdown_links_and_images_from_the_definition]` is also marked for this requirement, though it checks link rebasing rather than the back-links.\n\n**Reference badges still link to the declaration**\n`src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[references_in_nested_chapters_link_to_the_requirement_definition]` checks that impl, cite and test badges in a nested chapter link to `../requirements.html#habeas-req-requirements.ready`.\n\n**Names containing `.md`**\n- `fn[links_preserve_requirement_names_containing_md]` asserts that `chapter_href` produces `%2Emd`-escaped names for both the detail link and the anchored definition link.\n- `fn[links_to_readme_chapters_use_the_index_output]` covers README chapters.\n- The `cli.mdbook` fixtures in `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages` and `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` check the escaped anchor id, the name link and the \"View definition\" link end to end.\n\nI found no obligation that lacks a test with an assertion on its outcome. I found no applicable {fixme}.",
